      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "istolethetv from Hong Kong, China",
      "description": "There are thousands of domestic helpers in Hong Kong. They tend to be either Phillipine, Thai, or Indonesian. Most of them only have Sunday off, and on that day they cluster in parks and other public places around town. Victoria Park Causeway Bay is where the Indonesian women usually go. Several industries have popped up because of this phenomenon, including outdoor portrait studios. They provide fancy clothes and costumes, accessories, and backdrops with beautiful scenes. The women get done up and have their pictures taken. It must be nice to feel fussed over and made to feel glamorous after spending 6 days a week cooking, taking care of babies, and cleaning houses.",
